				<string name="Value"><![CDATA[CURSED DISTRICT — TOKYO
JJK-inspired Roblox progression prototype. Original block-built map and enemy art.

OPEN
Open Cursed_District_Tokyo.rbxlx in Roblox Studio, then press Play (F5).
Choose Sorcerer or Cursed Spirit. Your Roblox display name is your character name.
Walk to the mentor near spawn and use E. Accept the training-yard mission.
Walk west (left from the road-facing spawn) to defeat the Wandering Curses.

CONTROLS
WASD move; Space jump; standard Roblox camera controls.
Left click or 1: basic melee combo. Q: rolled technique (25 energy, 5-second cooldown).
R: domain burst (Level 12, 70 energy, 30-second cooldown).
F: hold to block frontal attacks. Touch: use the on-screen buttons; block toggles.
E / proximity prompt: NPC conversation. STATS button: view character details.
Face enemies to attack. Step out of red warning circles before attacks land.

WORLD
A 720-by-720-stud solid land base with roads, sidewalks, a safe plaza, modeled
buildings/windows, lamps, trees, training yard, cemetery, station, and shrine.
All combat areas are on the ground. A physical boundary keeps players on the map.
Tokyo is playable. Kyoto, Sendai and Okinawa are clearly labeled future districts.

PROGRESSION
Starting technique weights: 40 / 25 / 15 / 10 / 7 / 3 percent.
Roles have different technique names; this starter shares combat mechanics and map.
Techniques currently use forward energy bursts with distinct range, power and color;
they do not implement the full anime abilities. Domain is an expanding damage burst.
Earn XP and yen from enemies and repeatable missions. Maximum level: 30.
Grades: Grade 5 at 1; Grade 4 at 3; Grade 3 at 6; Grade 2 at 10; Grade 1 at 16;
Special Grade requires Level 25 and at least 3 Shrine Warden victories.
Supplier sells damage and health upgrades (10 tiers each), plus full recovery.
Missions automatically pay on completion. Return to the mentor to accept another.
Death respawns you at the safe plaza without removing progress or yen.
Co-op contributors get rewards if they deal at least 5% of enemy maximum health
and are alive within 100 studs when the enemy dies. No PvP in this version.

SAVING
Studio intentionally uses session-only profiles; stopping the test resets progress.
Published servers save role, technique, XP, level, yen, upgrades, kills, boss victories
and mission progress to DataStoreService. Saves run every 45 seconds and on exit.
DataStore profiles use a 180-second session lease to reduce overlapping-server writes.
If loading fails, joining is stopped to avoid overwriting existing progress.
Persistent saving requires a published experience and must be tested there.
No paid items, external HTTP requests, toolbox assets, uploaded images or sounds.

EDIT
Workspace/TokyoDistrict: physical map.
Workspace/NPCs: Mentor, Supplier and Travel with ProximityPrompts.
Workspace/EnemySpawns: invisible enemy origin markers. Enemies appear during Play.
ReplicatedStorage/Config: techniques, enemy stats, missions and title.
ServerScriptService/Progression: levels, grades, XP, upgrade rules.
ServerScriptService/Persistence: profile saves.
ServerScriptService/DistrictServer: damage validation, AI, rewards, NPCs, sessions.
StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/DistrictClient: UI, input and local effects.
ServerStorage/START_HERE: this guide.

LIMITS AND TESTING
This is a playable starter, not a finished Blox Fruits-scale release. The models are
original stylized block figures, with no custom rig animations, music, or exact anime
character assets. Enemies chase within open combat courts; they do not navigate the
whole city. Published analytics, moderation tools and production movement anti-cheat
are not implemented. Damage/cooldowns/range/purchases/progression run on the server.
Lua syntax, progression/economy tests and XML structure were checked locally.
Roblox Studio is unavailable in the build environment: engine behavior, UI layout,
enemy feel, mobile input, two-player combat and live persistence need Studio testing.

FIRST TEST
1. Walk around the map. Confirm the ground, sidewalks and spawn have collision.
2. Pick a role; confirm a technique is assigned once and stats show Grade 5.
3. Accept the training mission and defeat 4 Wandering Curses. Check XP/yen payout.
4. Use Q, observe energy/cooldown, and confirm basic attacks work while Q cools down.
5. Block and step out of warning circles. Die once and verify progress is retained.
6. Buy an upgrade at the supplier; check currency and stats.
7. Test with two clients, including shared damage, missions, disconnects and respawn.
8. Publish privately and verify saving by leaving and rejoining before public release.

Implementation references:
https://create.roblox.com/docs/cloud-services/data-stores
